=== meta ===
rule: ASSERT_WEAKENED
title: a test parameter bound again under a condition is no plain local, so `result == 20.0` is not read as checking `area(4, 5)` and the precondition still takes the old `==`'s place
origin: #434 A, ruling 434 A (2026-10-16) - a unit parameter is excluded: when `exact` is false, `result` is the fixture's value, and `result == 20.0` no longer checks the code
=== before: tests/test_geometry.py ===
from app.geometry import area


def test_area():
    assert area(4, 5) == 20.0
=== after: tests/test_geometry.py ===
from app.geometry import area


def test_area(result, exact):
    if exact:
        result = area(4, 5)
    assert result is not None
    assert result == 20.0
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "ASSERT_WEAKENED", "severity": "high", "escalators": ["NO_PROD_CHANGE_IN_DIFF"]}]
